[Music]  [Music]  i sort of felt that i just wanted to  tell like a night in the life of batman  you know  what what does a monday night look like  for batman but then when we hit on the  idea of of the blackout that that was  when it was like oh okay  that's the that's the hook  it all came out of that simple idea  that that he's got to get from one side  of gotham to the other in total blackout  with no support like he's marooned  abandoned  and the entirety of gotham is kind of  trying to sort of uh  get on top of him disable him take him  out take out emp a new villain  so uh yeah it's a very  simple concept i guess you know but it  all just happens within one evening  emp is  he essentially  he feeds on energy you know so that can  be electricity  um it can be emotional energy but he  can't really control it so he's been  subdued in arkham for years and years  they're basically transporting him from  the old  um  maybe slightly outdated uh arkham asylum  to the new facility black gay prison so  he's traveling in this kind of faraday  cage which is like a you know a box that  keeps the energy kind of contained  but you know without giving too much  away things go wrong he's a very  volatile character basically and and  and batman having to to get this guy  from one side to the other you know  during this kind of crazy night is um is  a challenge  it's a different muscle to flex for sure  you know um i've been lucky that i've  worked with them some of the best  writers in comics but um  yeah this is something different and and  it's definitely more challenging but  it's all the more uh rewarding for it i  find drawing the thumbnails is how i  write the script essentially  um i write a little uh outline of what's  going to  occur in in the issue and and then i  basically get to  to to doing the layout so and that's how  i can figure out the pace and and the  rhythm and the size of the scenes and  how how they all fit together  i'm not sure i'm quite why i just sit  down at a typewriter you know and  literally write us you know  30 page script and then then sit down  and draw it even though when i that's  what i receive from other writers i feel  like for for this thing um  it sort of suits my  just the way i do things that  i i sort of write it by drawing it you  know and i edit a lot and take stuff out  and everything else and i move pages  around and panels around but but i'm  essentially um i'm much more comfortable  telling the story visually that's uh  seemed to be the the way that it's  worked best for me  yeah i do love using black and what  better character is there to use black  on than batman you know i feel like  so many times when i've drawn him you  sort of do quite a lot of underdrawing  and the more black you add the he tends  to just look better and better and  better until you're just left with that  you know iconic silhouette that that we  all know  with the two piercing eyes and as if he  wasn't black enough you know i've called  this book one dark knight and it's set  during a blackout so it's there's even  more black  in this book which which sounds like you  know it could be easier but it's  actually super challenging to make that  work in a really effective way  one page that uh  remained exactly the same from the  tiniest little thumbnail when i had the  idea to the inks to the color and and  it's you know in the very early stages  of batman chasing emp across gotham it  has a huge bat symbol kind of you know  on city hall you know it was one of  those pages where i could see it  immediately and and i'm pleased to say  the final art kind of you know which is  quite rare for me i was i was kind of  reasonably happy with it so um that was  the page that really kind of summed up  the initial kind of you know momentum of  the story and it was a lot of fun to  draw  [Music]  [Music]  you know the evening that it got  announced you know but i was sort of you  know my phone was lit up for hours and  hours and hours it was it was uh you  know this is a story that's very dear to  my heart and then i put so so much into  it so to get that kind of response from  you know hopefully people are looking  forward to seeing the book it was just  you know the icing on on the cake for me  i've spent the last  year already on on this story um i'm  putting everything i've got  into it and yeah i can't wait for  everyone to see it  [Applause]  [Music]  you

